lrzsz (0.12.21rc-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a series of security-related bugs. Thanks to Daniel Birtwhistle for
    bringing these to our attention and for his support during patch
    verification:
    * 01-rz-reject-absolute-paths.diff: reject sender-supplied absolute paths
      in rz restricted mode.
    * 02-rz-terminate-received-strings.diff: reject over-length received file
      names, fixing an out-of-bounds read and a one-byte heap overwrite on
      maximum-length ZFILE names; also terminate the receiver buffer.
    * 03-rz-junk-path-double-free.diff: fix a double-free and a use-after-free
      when a --junk-path name ends in '/'.
    * 04-rz-null-flag-use-after-free.diff: fix use-after-free with -D/--null.

