lrzsz (0.12.21rc-3) unstable; urgency=low

  * Drop the lsz.1 documentation of the sz -T/-TT test and diagnostic modes.
    These were inherited from Chuck Forsberg's original sz but do not exist in
    lrzsz, where -T is bound solely to --turbo. A user following the manual's
    "sz -TT" diagnosis instructions therefore only ran --turbo twice and got a
    normal, failing transfer to the terminal. Add new patch
    618357_manpage_remove_test_mode.diff removing the stale -TT synopsis form,
    the "sixth form" paragraph, the "TESTING FEATURE" section and the orphaned
    BUGS sentence, closes: #618357.
  * Clarify in lsz.1 that the advertised YMODEM-g support only applies when the
    receiving program requests it (by sending 'G'), and that lrzsz's own rb/rz
    cannot do so, hence a separate receiver is required. This explains why the
    feature seemed missing. Add new patch 206499_ymodemg_doc.diff,
    closes: #206499.
  * Make debian/watch usable again. ohse.de does not index the packaged
    0.12.21rc tarball on any browsable page, but upstream's GitHub repository
    README links it directly; scan that page for the release and fetch the
    tarball from its canonical ohse.de location.

 -- Martin A. Godisch <godisch@debian.org>  Fri, 19 Jun 2026 05:56:36 +0200

lrzsz (0.12.21rc-2) unstable; urgency=low

  * Fix FTBFS with "make --shuffle=reverse". The upstream src/Makefile.am
    install-exec-local hook hard-links the installed binaries but does not
    depend on install-binPROGRAMS, so under shuffled prerequisite order it ran
    before the binaries were installed and ln aborted. Add new patch
    1105467_shuffle_install_order.diff declaring the dependency explicitly,
    closes: #1105467.
  * Keep syslog timestamps locale-independent. setlocale(LC_ALL, "") in lrz/lsz
    also set LC_TIME, which the C library's syslog() used for the message
    timestamp, so log lines from sz/rz showed a translated month name while the
    rest of the log stayed English. Add new patch
    57884_syslog_locale_timestamp.diff resetting LC_TIME to "C", closes: #57884.
  * Fix the XMODEM "Blocks received" counter for files larger than 255 blocks.
    wcrx() displayed the raw one-byte block number, which wraps at 255, so the
    on-screen count restarted at 0 (showing "055", "155", ... due to the
    carriage-return redraw) instead of continuing 256, 257, ... Add new patch
    156249_xmodem_block_counter.diff reporting the running sector total instead,
    closes: #156249.
  * Silence the only remaining C compiler warning: siginterrupt() is deprecated
    (-Wdeprecated-declarations). Add new patch fix_siginterrupt_deprecation.diff
    installing the SIGALRM handlers via sigaction() with sa_flags = 0 instead,
    preserving the "interrupt blocking syscalls on timeout" behaviour.
  * Bump Standards-Version to 4.7.4 (no further changes required).
  * Switch to debhelper compat level 13.
  * Add ${misc:Depends} to the binary package's Depends.
  * Update debian/watch to format version 4.
  * Refresh the debian/copyright header (current maintainer, upstream URL).
  * Packaging QA: add DEP-3 Description/Forwarded headers to all quilt patches;
    drop the obsolete debian/source/include-binaries (its entries no longer
    exist in the tree) and the stray, non-series patch
    206499_ymodemg.diff.unchecked.

 -- Martin A. Godisch <godisch@debian.org>  Thu, 18 Jun 2026 14:02:51 +0200

lrzsz (0.12.21rc-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix FTBFS with gettext 0.26 / modern autopoint. configure.in used
    AM_GNU_GETTEXT without any version declaration, so autopoint assumed the
    obsolete gettext-0.10.32 infrastructure and aborted autoreconf. Add new
    patch gettext_require_version.diff declaring
    AM_GNU_GETTEXT_REQUIRE_VERSION([0.19.8]), closes: #1126976, #1136751.
  * The modern gettext infrastructure pulled in that way needs po/Makevars
    and po/LINGUAS, which upstream never shipped. Add both via new patch
    po_makevars_linguas.diff (LINGUAS lists "de" to keep the German
    catalogue).
  * Make "debian/rules clean" idempotent. dh_autoreconf installs automake's
    maintainer-mode rebuild rules, so a second build re-ran automake during
    "make clean" and failed (automake >= 1.16 rejects the old configure.in).
    Neutralise ACLOCAL/AUTOCONF/AUTOMAKE/AUTOHEADER for that clean invocation.
  * Also remove the configure/config.status output (Makefile, config.h,
    config.status, sub-directory Makefiles, Specfile, systype, ...) in the
    clean target. "make clean" left these behind, so a rebuild aborted in
    dpkg-source -b with unexpected changes to the 3.0 (quilt) tree.
  * Fix the remaining C compiler warnings via new patch compiler_warnings.diff:
    a real -Wformat= bug in src/lsyslog.c (int passed for %ld) and the
    -Wunused-result warnings for write()/system()/vasprintf() in src/.

